  {
    "id": "experience-2",
    "section": "experience",
    "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant - Medical Imaging and Deep Learning",
    "content": "NED University of Engineering and Technology, Karachi. Faculty supervisor: Dr. Usman Amjad. September 2026 to present. - I research 3D deformable, featureless image registration to track how chronic wounds change over time. This is part of a federally funded HEC/NRPU research project. - Because no public chronic-wound-progression dataset exists, I test and validate the registration approach on two proxy datasets: BraTS-Reg (brain MRI, pre-operative vs follow-up scans with expert landmark ground truth) and Skin3D / 3DBodyTex (textured 3D skin-surface meshes). - I independently benchmark registration accuracy across both datasets, working toward applying the method to real wound-progression data.",
