    "id": "projects-2",
    "section": "projects",
    "title": "Sentinel AI - Live Scam Call Detection",
    "content": "GIKI Advanced AI Bootcamp 2026 capstone, team of 3. - Problem: scam phone calls trick people in real time, before they realise what is happening. - What we built: a real-time scam-call detection system using a multi-agent LangGraph pipeline with 6 specialised workers: pattern detection, semantic matching, emotional-manipulation analysis, social-engineering analysis, organisation verification and compliance scoring. Backend: FastAPI with WebSockets. Frontend: React + Electron. - My role: I owned the frontend, the UI and testing, including fixing a live microphone input bug. - Result: presented to the GIKI Rector as a winning-project showcase. - Code: https://github.com/Hassan-Raza-Shaikh/Live-Scam-Calling-Detection",
